  "createdAt" : 1757971336,
  "description" : "This dataset contains the number and percent of students at each proficiency level in four composite areas of the ACCESS for ELLs test (Oral Language, Literacy, Comprehension, Overall) from 2022 onward.\n\nMassachusetts administers the ACCESS for ELLs test annually to all English learners in publicly funded K-12 schools, as required by state and federal law.\n\nThe test evaluates students in the four subdomains of speaking, listening, reading, and writing. In addition to scores for each subdomain, results are reported in composite scores for comprehension, oral language, literacy, and overall English proficiency. Composite scores are created from two or more domain scores in listening, speaking, reading, and writing. Only students who complete all four domains of the standard test are included in composite scores.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/access.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ACCESS for ELLs Composite Proficiency Level Report</a>",
